1
00:00:04,315 --> 00:00:06,415
(Love In Sync)

2
00:00:13,255 --> 00:00:15,725
(Kim Myung Soo)

3
00:00:19,865 --> 00:00:22,395
(Kang Min Ah)

4
00:00:42,115 --> 00:00:45,285
(Love In Sync)

5
00:00:47,125 --> 00:00:48,194
(All people, incidents, and backgrounds...)

6
00:00:48,195 --> 00:00:49,324
(in this drama are fictitious and unrelated to reality.)

7
00:00:49,325 --> 00:00:50,525
(Also, children and animals were filmed under production guidelines.)

8
00:00:50,995 --> 00:00:52,725
After Shin Mi Jeong exposed Ji An's bullying,

9
00:00:53,125 --> 00:00:55,135
her mother passed away not long after.

10
00:00:55,635 --> 00:00:59,335
- Her mother? - She was already battling cancer.

11
00:00:59,905 --> 00:01:01,575
It seems her mother was her only family.

12
00:01:02,375 --> 00:01:03,505
It's a shame, especially at her young age.

13
00:01:04,245 --> 00:01:06,045
Anyway, she's been a recluse ever since.

14
00:01:06,305 --> 00:01:07,445
There's no record of her whereabouts.

15
00:01:08,045 --> 00:01:09,315
And her place of residence is unclear.

16
00:01:10,915 --> 00:01:11,915
Really?

17
00:01:12,785 --> 00:01:13,785
But who do you think you're talking to?

18
00:01:14,585 --> 00:01:16,685
I went to the hospital where her mother was admitted,

19
00:01:17,225 --> 00:01:19,755
and told them to contact me if Mi Jeong shows up.

20
00:01:20,285 --> 00:01:21,295
So let's just wait.

21
00:01:21,855 --> 00:01:23,665
They said her mother's things were still there.

22
00:01:24,065 --> 00:01:26,065
She wouldn't just throw away her mom's keepsakes, right?

23
00:01:36,175 --> 00:01:37,175
You're back?

24
00:01:38,075 --> 00:01:39,075
Yes.

25
00:01:40,745 --> 00:01:42,775
- Where's Ha Yul? - She's asleep.

26
00:01:42,845 --> 00:01:43,845
Sorry, Song Hwan.

27
00:01:43,915 --> 00:01:45,945
I haven't been much help lately, have I?

28
00:01:46,245 --> 00:01:48,285
It's fine. It'll be over soon anyway.

29
00:01:50,885 --> 00:01:51,885
Get some rest.

30
00:01:52,955 --> 00:01:53,955
Oh, right.

31
00:01:54,695 --> 00:01:55,695
You got some mail.

32
00:02:05,835 --> 00:02:08,005
(Korea Psychological Counselling Association)

33
00:02:08,075 --> 00:02:10,605
(Notice of Nullification of Disciplinary Action)

34
00:02:34,765 --> 00:02:35,765
Is she cold?

35
00:02:44,345 --> 00:02:47,515
What? Why are you glaring at me? Why?

36
00:02:49,445 --> 00:02:50,745
I wasn't glaring.

37
00:02:51,485 --> 00:02:53,285
Hey, I was just looking.

38
00:02:53,785 --> 00:02:55,515
Then why were you looking at me?

39
00:02:56,055 --> 00:02:57,055
It was creepy.

40
00:02:57,555 --> 00:02:58,625
Jeez.

41
00:03:03,295 --> 00:03:04,295
Here.

42
00:03:05,325 --> 00:03:06,525
Is this your first winter shoot?

43
00:03:07,135 --> 00:03:08,865
You should be prepared for things like this.

44
00:03:09,365 --> 00:03:10,705
You were just as unprepared when you were an idol.

45
00:03:26,245 --> 00:03:27,255
It's...

46
00:03:30,525 --> 00:03:31,525
Sorry.

47
00:03:32,455 --> 00:03:33,455
What?

48
00:03:34,695 --> 00:03:35,695
I...

49
00:03:37,495 --> 00:03:38,865
I said I'm sorry.

50
00:03:40,835 --> 00:03:41,835
For what?

51
00:03:42,135 --> 00:03:43,495
Just, you know...

52
00:03:45,635 --> 00:03:47,175
For everything.

53
00:03:50,545 --> 00:03:51,545
Are you sick or something?

54
00:03:53,445 --> 00:03:54,445
You're unbelievable.

55
00:03:56,645 --> 00:03:57,845
Anyway, I apologised.

56
00:04:10,195 --> 00:04:11,195
Hello.

57
00:04:15,695 --> 00:04:16,695
This is Mi Jeong, right?

58
00:04:17,265 --> 00:04:18,265
Where are you right now?

59
00:04:19,005 --> 00:04:20,905
This is the scene where your anger toward each other...

60
00:04:20,975 --> 00:04:21,975
reaches its peak.

61
00:04:22,475 --> 00:04:24,975
It's one of the most pivotal scenes in the story,

62
00:04:25,405 --> 00:04:26,905
so I need you both to really focus.

63
00:04:27,715 --> 00:04:30,374
- Yes. - But your chemistry is fantastic,

64
00:04:30,375 --> 00:04:31,845
so I'm not worried about that, right?

65
00:04:36,085 --> 00:04:38,425
All right. Let's take a short break, and then we'll start filming.

66
00:04:39,225 --> 00:04:40,325
- Okay. - Okay.

67
00:05:01,945 --> 00:05:02,945
Here.

68
00:05:08,755 --> 00:05:09,755
Are you nervous?

69
00:05:10,655 --> 00:05:13,085
Of course. It's the highlight of the movie.

70
00:05:14,425 --> 00:05:17,265
And it's my first major scene with Yi Jin.

71
00:05:18,925 --> 00:05:20,025
She's a great actress, you know.

72
00:05:21,165 --> 00:05:23,135
It would be embarrassing if I'm the only one who bombs.

73
00:05:27,935 --> 00:05:28,935
Are you feeling okay?

74
00:05:29,005 --> 00:05:30,505
You seemed to have a cold this morning.

75
00:05:31,845 --> 00:05:33,475
That's why I said you should go to the doctor.

76
00:05:34,645 --> 00:05:36,174
What if I get drowsy from the medicine...

77
00:05:36,175 --> 00:05:38,745
- right before a shoot? - You're a real pro now.

78
00:05:39,515 --> 00:05:42,655
I was always a pro. It's just that no one noticed.

79
00:05:52,665 --> 00:05:53,665
One moment.

80
00:05:56,165 --> 00:05:57,165
Yes, Detective.

81
00:05:58,235 --> 00:05:59,235
Yes.

82
00:06:00,435 --> 00:06:01,435
Shin Mi Jeong?

83
00:06:03,205 --> 00:06:04,845
Yes, I understand. I'll head over right now.

84
00:06:05,505 --> 00:06:06,505
Okay, thank you.

85
00:06:09,115 --> 00:06:10,575
What's so serious?

86
00:06:11,185 --> 00:06:13,815
I heard that Shin Mi Jeong showed up at the hospital.

87
00:06:14,285 --> 00:06:15,285
Mi Jeong?

88
00:06:15,615 --> 00:06:17,055
I think I have to go right now.

89
00:06:17,325 --> 00:06:19,285
Right now? But the shoot is about to start.

90
00:06:19,385 --> 00:06:21,125
This is a really important scene.

91
00:06:21,455 --> 00:06:23,655
Don't worry. It's not far from here.

92
00:06:24,295 --> 00:06:25,295
I'll be back soon.

93
00:06:26,665 --> 00:06:29,635
Even if I'm late, now...

94
00:06:31,235 --> 00:06:32,665
you'll be able to do it on your own.

95
00:06:33,975 --> 00:06:36,635
- What? - Believe in yourself.

96
00:06:52,755 --> 00:06:56,625
(132 Ga 4819)

97
00:07:20,345 --> 00:07:21,815
Why isn't he coming even now?

98
00:07:23,455 --> 00:07:26,525
All right, let's start shooting. Everyone on standby.

99
00:07:31,465 --> 00:07:33,495
You're always so cruel, Detective.

100
00:07:34,295 --> 00:07:37,635
- What? - I've heard a lot about you.

101
00:07:38,105 --> 00:07:39,865
And how you conduct your investigations.

102
00:07:41,075 --> 00:07:42,075
Like a game...

103
00:07:42,375 --> 00:07:44,405
I heard you treated your cases like a game.

104
00:07:45,805 --> 00:07:47,715
You solve them, but you miss what's important.

105
00:07:47,775 --> 00:07:49,145
And you did it again, didn't you?

106
00:07:49,775 --> 00:07:51,115
You said I knew everything.

107
00:07:51,445 --> 00:07:52,785
You said I was the mastermind of this game.

108
00:07:54,055 --> 00:07:55,055
You're wrong.

109
00:07:55,755 --> 00:07:57,625
Everything you assumed was wrong.

110
00:08:12,505 --> 00:08:13,505
You...

111
00:08:15,035 --> 00:08:17,275
You knew exactly what Lim Jun Ho did.

112
00:08:18,045 --> 00:08:19,745
And you played all of us to cover for him.

113
00:08:20,745 --> 00:08:22,444
Because I was arrogant enough to think I had figured out...

114
00:08:22,445 --> 00:08:25,785
about you, the people I care about got hurt.

115
00:08:27,555 --> 00:08:29,655
If you think you're the only one who's suffered through all this,

116
00:08:29,715 --> 00:08:30,715
you're sorely mistaken.

117
00:08:31,655 --> 00:08:34,925
That's why I'm going to solve this, no matter what.

118
00:08:35,925 --> 00:08:38,995
Even if it means I have to take a completely different approach.

119
00:08:42,865 --> 00:08:43,865
Cut, okay.

120
00:09:47,025 --> 00:09:48,035
Are you awake?

121
00:09:49,735 --> 00:09:52,165
You should have told me you had such a high fever.

122
00:09:53,565 --> 00:09:54,805
Excuse me, the patient here...

123
00:09:58,405 --> 00:09:59,405
Don't go.

124
00:10:01,245 --> 00:10:02,245
Don't go.

125
00:10:05,215 --> 00:10:06,615
I said don't go.

126
00:10:26,365 --> 00:10:28,305
- Why are you calling? - Hey, I found him.

127
00:10:28,975 --> 00:10:30,335
I found Kim Min Su.

128
00:10:32,205 --> 00:10:33,775
(Scene 31, Hospital Hall, Night, Jeong Min Standing with a Phone)

129
00:10:33,845 --> 00:10:35,044
He's overseas right now,

130
00:10:35,045 --> 00:10:36,445
so he said he didn't know about Ji An's situation.

131
00:10:37,045 --> 00:10:39,615
If you look at the original script he gave me,

132
00:10:40,545 --> 00:10:43,115
the lines are identical to Ji An's bullying video.

133
00:10:47,895 --> 00:10:49,054
He also said...

134
00:10:49,055 --> 00:10:52,225
that he had the screen test footage for Ji An's part.

135
00:10:52,365 --> 00:10:54,465
He said he'd send it over no matter how long it takes if we want.

136
00:10:55,365 --> 00:10:57,165
He must have been secretly grateful to Ji An.

137
00:10:57,605 --> 00:10:59,905
Well, he was an unknown director, but she didn't ignore him,

138
00:11:00,365 --> 00:11:01,575
and agreed to be in his movie.

139
00:11:03,235 --> 00:11:06,675
So, if we get the original script and the screen test footage,

140
00:11:07,915 --> 00:11:10,215
won't that clear Ji An of the false bullying accusation right away?

141
00:11:12,345 --> 00:11:14,585
And if we find out who was behind this,

142
00:11:16,355 --> 00:11:17,355
it'll all be over.

143
00:11:21,525 --> 00:11:23,955
(Detective)

144
00:11:39,045 --> 00:11:40,345
Do Hoon, hold on.

145
00:11:41,315 --> 00:11:42,315
This is Yi Jin's...

146
00:11:45,345 --> 00:11:46,885
Why doesn't he ever listen?

147
00:11:55,095 --> 00:11:56,095
Mr. Cha.

148
00:11:56,855 --> 00:12:00,665
So I checked Shin Mi Jeong's bank records just in case,

149
00:12:01,395 --> 00:12:02,534
and I found out a large sum of money was deposited...

150
00:12:02,535 --> 00:12:03,935
right before the scandal broke.

151
00:12:05,305 --> 00:12:07,405
The depositor was Han Yi Jin.

152
00:12:09,105 --> 00:12:13,705
Why would Yi Jin send her so much money?

153
00:12:17,945 --> 00:12:18,945
I think...

154
00:12:19,715 --> 00:12:20,985
I think there's another culprit.

155
00:12:22,155 --> 00:12:23,185
Is that really true?

156
00:12:23,455 --> 00:12:24,684
Are you sure Yi Jin has been in contact...

157
00:12:24,685 --> 00:12:26,355
with Shin Mi Jeong?

158
00:12:26,555 --> 00:12:28,355
Well, I don't know if they're in contact,

159
00:12:28,625 --> 00:12:29,995
but I saw her on the phone with her a few times.

160
00:12:30,625 --> 00:12:32,894
On top of that, Yi Jin was the one...

161
00:12:32,895 --> 00:12:36,095
who connected Ji An to that thug, CEO Noh.

162
00:12:37,135 --> 00:12:38,165
If you think about it,

163
00:12:38,635 --> 00:12:40,635
Yi Jin is a more likely suspect than the CEO, isn't she?

164
00:12:41,375 --> 00:12:42,835
They've been enemies from the start.

165
00:12:43,505 --> 00:12:46,075
- That's why the bullying video... - Is that really true?

166
00:12:49,615 --> 00:12:51,345
Did Yi Jin really do that to me?

167
00:12:59,685 --> 00:13:00,685
Ji An.

168
00:13:06,125 --> 00:13:07,125
Ji An.

169
00:13:10,495 --> 00:13:11,765
(Actress Han Yi Jin's Dressing Room)

170
00:13:13,635 --> 00:13:14,635
Ji An.

171
00:13:23,775 --> 00:13:26,485
We were in the middle of shooting a vlog.

172
00:13:33,455 --> 00:13:37,055
Gosh, now there's even an assault on set.

173
00:13:37,255 --> 00:13:39,865
I've been in this business for a long time,

174
00:13:39,925 --> 00:13:43,165
but this is a first. What are you going to do now?

175
00:13:44,235 --> 00:13:47,335
Hey, someone else did the hitting,

176
00:13:47,405 --> 00:13:49,805
so why are you blaming the innocent Director Moon?

177
00:13:50,005 --> 00:13:52,674
I was so against it, but he insisted on casting her.

178
00:13:52,675 --> 00:13:54,415
He has to take responsibility.

179
00:13:55,915 --> 00:13:57,115
How should I take responsibility?

180
00:13:59,145 --> 00:14:00,685
Fire Yu Ji An.

181
00:14:01,085 --> 00:14:04,054
Wait, if we fire Yu Ji An now,

182
00:14:04,055 --> 00:14:05,725
what about the production costs for what we've already filmed?

183
00:14:05,925 --> 00:14:07,325
That's not my problem.

184
00:14:07,525 --> 00:14:10,695
How can the attacker and the victim act in the same space?

185
00:14:10,755 --> 00:14:12,325
This is secondary victimization.

186
00:14:12,725 --> 00:14:15,495
CEO Kim, please. Let's all calm down first.

187
00:14:15,565 --> 00:14:17,165
CEO Kim does have a point.

188
00:14:19,405 --> 00:14:22,675
I also feel that what happened on my set...

189
00:14:22,975 --> 00:14:24,335
was deeply regrettable.

190
00:14:27,505 --> 00:14:30,145
For now, let's suspend Yu Ji An's filming.

191
00:14:30,515 --> 00:14:33,245
We'll figure out the next steps as we go.

192
00:14:35,215 --> 00:14:36,285
Director Moon.

193
00:14:36,915 --> 00:14:39,525
Come on, Director Moon, don't be too enraged.

194
00:14:45,095 --> 00:14:46,794
Filming people to back them into a corner...

195
00:14:46,795 --> 00:14:47,865
must be your hobby.

196
00:14:49,495 --> 00:14:50,635
But what a shame.

197
00:14:51,705 --> 00:14:53,704
I don't think you'll be able to enjoy...

198
00:14:53,705 --> 00:14:55,635
that little hobby of yours anymore.

199
00:14:57,945 --> 00:14:59,575
Because I'm going to make sure to block you.

200
00:15:16,295 --> 00:15:18,465
Since there's no filming for a while anyway,

201
00:15:19,025 --> 00:15:20,465
you don't have to come in starting tomorrow.

202
00:15:21,765 --> 00:15:23,764
No, scratch that. Since it looks like...

203
00:15:23,765 --> 00:15:25,135
I won't be able to make a comeback,

204
00:15:26,405 --> 00:15:28,075
why don't we just terminate our contract?

205
00:15:31,305 --> 00:15:33,005
That's what you wanted, right?

206
00:15:36,115 --> 00:15:37,115
Then, goodbye.

207
00:15:46,555 --> 00:15:48,555
I told you to leave. Why are you still standing there?

208
00:15:50,125 --> 00:15:51,495
I said go. Go.

209
00:15:52,065 --> 00:15:53,665
You were so desperate to leave.

210
00:15:54,165 --> 00:15:56,095
- Ji An... - Just get out.

211
00:15:57,665 --> 00:15:58,705
What did I do?

212
00:16:02,105 --> 00:16:04,005
What did I do that was so wrong?

213
00:16:06,375 --> 00:16:09,045
Why is everyone so eager to leave me?

214
00:16:11,015 --> 00:16:13,545
People, CEO Kim,

215
00:16:14,915 --> 00:16:15,955
Mi Jeong,

216
00:16:17,115 --> 00:16:18,225
and Yi Jin.

217
00:16:19,325 --> 00:16:20,325
Why?

218
00:16:21,325 --> 00:16:22,325
Why?

219
00:16:25,465 --> 00:16:27,995
You're just going to abandon me in the end anyway.

220
00:16:29,035 --> 00:16:30,065
So...

221
00:16:31,405 --> 00:16:33,165
just get out of here now.

222
00:16:38,405 --> 00:16:40,045
When you're hurting like this,

223
00:16:41,545 --> 00:16:42,715
how could I possibly leave?

224
00:16:57,125 --> 00:16:58,625
So don't leave.

225
00:17:00,425 --> 00:17:04,465
Don't abandon me, Cha Eun Hwan.

226
00:17:06,905 --> 00:17:07,905
Please.

227
00:17:48,175 --> 00:17:49,275
I told you, didn't I?

228
00:17:49,615 --> 00:17:52,715
That I'd make sure you make a successful comeback.

229
00:17:53,345 --> 00:17:55,715
Just trust me and wait a little longer.

230
00:17:56,115 --> 00:17:57,515
And make sure you eat.

231
00:18:27,985 --> 00:18:30,155
He's really terrible at cooking.

232
00:19:02,115 --> 00:19:03,855
(Phone)

233
00:19:03,955 --> 00:19:05,825
(Mom)

234
00:19:08,755 --> 00:19:12,895
(Mom)

235
00:19:20,805 --> 00:19:26,075
(My Daughter)

236
00:19:31,615 --> 00:19:32,784
The party you are trying to reach is unavailable.

237
00:19:32,785 --> 00:19:34,285
You will be connected to their voicemail...

238
00:19:44,295 --> 00:19:45,295
(The Late Park Yoon Hee)

239
00:19:45,296 --> 00:19:46,425
(Born: October 17, 1972, Died: January 24, 2026)

240
00:19:53,005 --> 00:19:54,975
Who are you?

241
00:20:00,005 --> 00:20:01,145
Ms. Shin Mi Jeong?

242
00:20:05,245 --> 00:20:06,384
I came because I thought you might be here...

243
00:20:06,385 --> 00:20:07,545
for your mother's memorial.

244
00:20:08,215 --> 00:20:10,915
- I'm glad I found you. - Who are you?

245
00:20:11,655 --> 00:20:13,125
I'm Yu Ji An's manager.

246
00:20:17,555 --> 00:20:20,765
First, I'm very sorry for your loss.

247
00:20:22,235 --> 00:20:23,765
You must have been through so much.

248
00:20:25,135 --> 00:20:29,235
I know exactly why you're here, but it's no use.

249
00:20:30,175 --> 00:20:32,405
I don't want to get involved in that case anymore.

250
00:20:32,905 --> 00:20:36,475
Call me selfish and awful, but there's nothing I can do.

251
00:20:37,875 --> 00:20:40,085
As for clearing Ji An of the bullying accusation,

252
00:20:41,385 --> 00:20:43,355
I already have enough evidence to do that.

253
00:20:45,655 --> 00:20:46,655
It's just that...

254
00:20:49,095 --> 00:20:51,095
the reason I came to find you, Mi Jeong,

255
00:20:52,125 --> 00:20:55,165
was in the hope of sparing Ji An some pain.

256
00:20:57,495 --> 00:20:58,605
That's all.

257
00:21:01,035 --> 00:21:02,035
Ji An...

258
00:21:03,175 --> 00:21:04,905
Is she having a hard time?

259
00:21:06,305 --> 00:21:08,845
Being betrayed by someone you trusted...

260
00:21:09,415 --> 00:21:11,245
is a pretty terrible thing.

261
00:21:13,245 --> 00:21:14,815
I'm not going to force you.

262
00:21:16,455 --> 00:21:17,885
The choice is yours to make.

263
00:21:19,485 --> 00:21:20,525
I'll be on my way, then.

264
00:21:21,855 --> 00:21:22,855
Wait.

265
00:21:23,825 --> 00:21:26,525
He said he'd introduce me to a doctor who could save my mom.

266
00:21:27,665 --> 00:21:28,835
CEO Kim said that.

267
00:21:30,835 --> 00:21:32,565
I didn't betray her for money.

268
00:21:33,965 --> 00:21:35,075
I really didn't.

269
00:21:45,185 --> 00:21:46,345
Darn it.

270
00:21:47,045 --> 00:21:48,685
Filming people to back them into a corner...

271
00:21:48,755 --> 00:21:49,755
must be your hobby.

272
00:21:50,455 --> 00:21:51,985
I don't think you'll be able to enjoy...

273
00:21:52,055 --> 00:21:53,855
that little hobby of yours anymore.

274
00:21:56,755 --> 00:21:57,755
Fine.

275
00:21:58,565 --> 00:22:00,695
The best defence is a good offence.

276
00:22:05,635 --> 00:22:06,635
Hey, Manager Kim.

277
00:22:06,705 --> 00:22:08,305
Get the reporters together right now.

278
00:22:09,505 --> 00:22:11,945
Stop arguing and just do what I told you.

279
00:22:13,705 --> 00:22:16,645
(J.An Entertainment)

280
00:22:17,575 --> 00:22:20,345
The CEO is about to leave for a press conference right now.

281
00:22:22,055 --> 00:22:23,084
I think he's planning...

282
00:22:23,085 --> 00:22:24,985
to completely frame Ji An for assault.

283
00:22:25,625 --> 00:22:26,825
Don't worry.

284
00:22:27,225 --> 00:22:29,895
Soon, nobody will believe a word that guy says.

285
00:22:37,095 --> 00:22:39,805
Fortunately, I'm only going to take down one guy.

286
00:22:40,365 --> 00:22:43,905
So I'll give you a chance to save your own skin, Reporter Han.

287
00:22:47,345 --> 00:22:49,315
This is the only piece of dirt I have on CEO Kim,

288
00:22:50,175 --> 00:22:51,275
but you, Reporter Han...

289
00:22:53,515 --> 00:22:54,915
I'm guessing it's a different story for you.

290
00:23:01,425 --> 00:23:03,855
He needs to feel how gut-wrenching betrayal is...

291
00:23:04,695 --> 00:23:05,865
for himself.

292
00:23:11,665 --> 00:23:13,364
(J.An Entertainment)

293
00:23:13,365 --> 00:23:15,035
Is everyone here? What about Yi Jin?

294
00:23:17,135 --> 00:23:19,144
Darn it. She needs to be here...

295
00:23:19,145 --> 00:23:22,175
and play the victim for this to be perfect.

296
00:23:23,515 --> 00:23:25,585
Apparently, a lot more reporters showed up than we expected.

297
00:23:25,815 --> 00:23:28,115
Really? I guess she still has pull.

298
00:23:28,185 --> 00:23:29,785
Even after hitting rock bottom, Yu Ji An still has clout.

299
00:23:31,455 --> 00:23:32,455
Let's go.

300
00:23:37,255 --> 00:23:39,295
What is this? Hey, CEO Won, what is it?

301
00:23:39,365 --> 00:23:40,425
I'm busy right now...

302
00:23:44,235 --> 00:23:45,235
What?

303
00:23:46,265 --> 00:23:47,835
Reporter Han? What's that bastard up to?

304
00:23:48,505 --> 00:23:49,505
Hey. Hold on.

305
00:23:53,575 --> 00:23:54,845
("Yu Ji An's Abuse of Power Controversy...")

306
00:23:54,905 --> 00:23:56,175
("Was A Scheme by the CEO of J.An Entertainment")

307
00:23:56,245 --> 00:23:57,375
Darn it.

308
00:24:02,455 --> 00:24:03,484
(A Confession)

309
00:24:03,485 --> 00:24:04,485
(Revealing the Truth Behind the Yu Ji An's Bullying Case)

310
00:24:05,125 --> 00:24:07,585
No matter what I say, or for what reason,

311
00:24:07,655 --> 00:24:09,454
I don't believe there are any excuses...

312
00:24:09,455 --> 00:24:11,195
for what I've done.

313
00:24:12,065 --> 00:24:15,795
I will humbly accept the consequences for my actions.

314
00:24:16,265 --> 00:24:19,335
Is your head just for decoration? You should try thinking for once...

315
00:24:22,175 --> 00:24:24,005
Am I being too calm to act like someone who's angry?

316
00:24:25,745 --> 00:24:27,075
Is your head just for decoration?

317
00:24:27,145 --> 00:24:28,775
You should try thinking for once...

318
00:24:29,115 --> 00:24:31,075
Oh? Hey, perfect timing.

319
00:24:31,945 --> 00:24:32,945
Again?

320
00:24:33,115 --> 00:24:35,584
You know, having someone to act with versus not,

321
00:24:35,585 --> 00:24:36,815
makes a difference getting in character.

322
00:24:37,555 --> 00:24:39,225
Don't half-heartedly do it like before.

323
00:24:39,285 --> 00:24:41,325
Act like you're really the one getting yelled at.

324
00:24:41,455 --> 00:24:42,725
That's how I can immerse myself in the role.

325
00:24:45,525 --> 00:24:48,565
Hey, where is your head at?

326
00:24:48,865 --> 00:24:50,265
How many times do I have to tell you?

327
00:24:50,965 --> 00:24:54,105
Is your head just for decoration? Do you even think at all?

328
00:24:54,405 --> 00:24:56,805
You have no idea what's going on, do you?

329
00:24:58,505 --> 00:25:00,775
Gosh. You're really driving me crazy.

330
00:25:01,075 --> 00:25:03,375
What is all this mess just because of one bad hire?

331
00:25:04,275 --> 00:25:07,515
Hey, I'm just asking because I'm genuinely curious,

332
00:25:07,815 --> 00:25:09,615
do your parents know you go around acting like this?

333
00:25:11,615 --> 00:25:14,825
Oh my, look at her. Are you crying?

334
00:25:15,155 --> 00:25:18,525
Hey, why are you crying? I said, why are you crying?

335
00:25:18,665 --> 00:25:21,095
Who do you think should be the one crying right now?

336
00:25:22,065 --> 00:25:24,835
I told you not to cry. Stop crying.

337
00:25:30,005 --> 00:25:32,875
Hey, wasn't my acting amazing?

338
00:25:33,545 --> 00:25:35,945
Wasn't that just total method acting?

339
00:25:36,275 --> 00:25:41,145
I know. You're really good at acting angry.

340
00:25:42,315 --> 00:25:44,955
Who says you can't act? You're so good...

341
00:25:48,625 --> 00:25:49,655
You act so good.

342
00:25:50,455 --> 00:25:51,925
You got the angles right, didn't you?

343
00:25:54,525 --> 00:25:56,595
- Bring it here so I can watch it. - Okay.

344
00:25:59,205 --> 00:26:00,335
Lastly,

345
00:26:00,565 --> 00:26:03,204
I want to say I'm sorry to Ji An,

346
00:26:03,205 --> 00:26:04,805
who was always so genuinely kind to me.

347
00:26:05,845 --> 00:26:06,845
Ji An.

348
00:26:07,875 --> 00:26:09,245
I'm truly sorry.

349
00:26:16,115 --> 00:26:18,055
I knew it. I believed in her all along.

350
00:26:18,215 --> 00:26:20,125
She's amazing for enduring all that. All the best.

351
00:26:20,185 --> 00:26:22,655
It's so sad to think of all the hate she got.

352
00:26:22,725 --> 00:26:26,425
- Wish you all the best from now on. - I'm glad the truth is finally out.

353
00:26:26,665 --> 00:26:30,135
She's a good actress too. Looks like she only has success ahead of her.

354
00:26:33,135 --> 00:26:34,135
I told you, didn't I?

355
00:26:35,135 --> 00:26:36,605
That you, Ji An, are absolutely...

356
00:26:38,775 --> 00:26:40,175
not that kind of person.

357
00:26:40,575 --> 00:26:42,475
So it really wasn't me.

358
00:26:43,575 --> 00:26:44,575
I...

359
00:26:45,445 --> 00:26:48,285
I was afraid that I might really be that kind of awful person.

360
00:26:52,685 --> 00:26:53,685
Thank you.

361
00:26:54,555 --> 00:26:55,555
For believing in me.

362
00:26:56,725 --> 00:26:57,895
For revealing the truth.

363
00:27:02,535 --> 00:27:03,565
If you're that grateful,

364
00:27:05,335 --> 00:27:08,435
will you grant me a wish?

365
00:27:13,075 --> 00:27:15,615
Is this really your wish? To spend the whole day with me?

366
00:27:16,445 --> 00:27:20,085
Well, I never specified that it had to be you, Ji An.

367
00:27:21,115 --> 00:27:22,955
Just like how other people hang out with their friends,

368
00:27:23,815 --> 00:27:25,584
I said I wanted to spend just one day...

369
00:27:25,585 --> 00:27:27,655
having fun without any worries.

370
00:27:29,495 --> 00:27:32,965
Because I've never been able to do that.

371
00:27:33,465 --> 00:27:34,465
Geez.

372
00:27:35,435 --> 00:27:39,735
If you want to go on a date with me, just be honest and say it.

373
00:27:41,165 --> 00:27:43,135
How many times do I have to tell you that you can't hide it?

374
00:27:44,005 --> 00:27:46,245
Are you dumb?

375
00:27:47,745 --> 00:27:48,745
I can hear everything, you know.

376
00:27:49,045 --> 00:27:50,615
I can feel everything, you know.

377
00:27:56,915 --> 00:27:58,755
Friends hold hands when they hang out these days.

378
00:27:59,455 --> 00:28:00,455
Didn't you know?

379
00:28:23,115 --> 00:28:24,175
It's okay.

380
00:28:37,095 --> 00:28:38,455
It's...

381
00:29:00,215 --> 00:29:02,015
- This or that? - That one.

382
00:29:11,695 --> 00:29:13,095
Oh, they are cherry blossoms.

383
00:29:13,925 --> 00:29:14,994
I've never been able to properly see...

384
00:29:14,995 --> 00:29:16,295
the cherry blossoms because of filming.

385
00:29:24,035 --> 00:29:25,035
Right now,

386
00:29:26,275 --> 00:29:28,475
I'm about to do the most selfish thing in my life.

387
00:29:30,475 --> 00:29:32,015
But just this once,

388
00:29:33,585 --> 00:29:34,815
will you look the other way?

389
00:30:39,685 --> 00:30:40,685
You're here.

390
00:30:43,115 --> 00:30:45,185
- What are you doing here? - What do you mean?

391
00:30:45,555 --> 00:30:47,325
Starting today, I'm your manager.

392
00:30:48,185 --> 00:30:50,994
- What? - Didn't you hear anything...

393
00:30:50,995 --> 00:30:52,055
from Mr. Cha?

394
00:30:53,795 --> 00:30:56,395
He came to me himself and asked me to take good care of you.

395
00:30:57,335 --> 00:30:59,235
- He said he's quitting. - He's quitting?

396
00:31:04,875 --> 00:31:08,945
The phone is turned off. Connecting to voicemail. After the beep...

397
00:31:10,345 --> 00:31:11,345
Where are you going?

398
00:31:26,495 --> 00:31:27,495
Where's Eun Hwan?

399
00:31:27,865 --> 00:31:30,095
- He's home, right? - He's not here.

400
00:31:31,365 --> 00:31:35,935
- He left early this morning. - Left? Where to?

401
00:31:36,335 --> 00:31:37,705
He didn't say anything to me.

402
00:31:38,075 --> 00:31:39,075
I wouldn't know.

403
00:31:40,075 --> 00:31:41,975
He left without telling me anything specific either.

404
00:31:44,775 --> 00:31:47,985
But he must have had his reasons for leaving like that.

405
00:31:49,615 --> 00:31:50,685
Reasons?

406
00:31:51,685 --> 00:31:54,255
- What... - Since they can never be together,

407
00:31:54,755 --> 00:31:58,355
wouldn't being together be more like a punishment for them?

408
00:31:58,995 --> 00:32:03,365
Right now, I'm about to do the most selfish thing in my life.

409
00:32:23,155 --> 00:32:25,925
Unable to connect. You will be forwarded to voicemail.

410
00:32:31,325 --> 00:32:33,965
Ji An, the interview is starting soon.

411
00:32:34,325 --> 00:32:35,795
He hasn't contacted you either, right?

412
00:32:36,295 --> 00:32:37,295
Mr. Cha?

413
00:32:38,595 --> 00:32:39,605
No.

414
00:32:39,835 --> 00:32:41,735
Ever since he suddenly came to me and asked me to take care of you,

415
00:32:42,805 --> 00:32:44,005
I haven't been able to contact him either.

416
00:32:52,515 --> 00:32:54,444
You must have had a very difficult time...

417
00:32:54,445 --> 00:32:56,355
with the abuse of power controversy.

418
00:32:56,855 --> 00:33:00,455
Weren't you upset with the public for being so quick to judge?

419
00:33:02,255 --> 00:33:03,255
I understand.

420
00:33:03,995 --> 00:33:04,995
Even I...

421
00:33:06,225 --> 00:33:08,125
found it hard to believe in myself.

422
00:33:10,165 --> 00:33:11,195
I'm not sure.

423
00:33:11,765 --> 00:33:14,135
He didn't really say anything to me before he left either.

424
00:33:14,665 --> 00:33:17,205
You don't really expect me to believe that, do you?

425
00:33:18,305 --> 00:33:19,774
There's no way he'd leave his sister and Ha Yul...

426
00:33:19,775 --> 00:33:21,075
without asking you for help.

427
00:33:22,045 --> 00:33:24,715
Tell me everything you know. Where is he now?

428
00:33:25,175 --> 00:33:26,345
Why is he suddenly acting like this?

429
00:33:27,885 --> 00:33:31,885
- Is he mad at me about something? - No.

430
00:33:32,325 --> 00:33:33,325
It's not that.

431
00:33:33,385 --> 00:33:35,385
Then what is it? Please, just tell me.

432
00:33:36,595 --> 00:33:37,955
I don't really know either.

433
00:33:38,055 --> 00:33:40,395
It just seems he has some things he needs to sort out.

434
00:33:42,835 --> 00:33:45,665
Sort out what?

435
00:34:09,595 --> 00:34:11,354
- Hello. - Hey, man.

436
00:34:11,355 --> 00:34:12,995
Thanks to you, there's no way I'm getting into heaven.

437
00:34:13,795 --> 00:34:15,465
How long do I have to play the bad guy?

438
00:34:15,965 --> 00:34:17,765
Do you have any idea how Ji An is doing right now?

439
00:34:19,335 --> 00:34:20,435
Is she having a hard time?

440
00:34:20,835 --> 00:34:21,835
Of course she is.

441
00:34:22,105 --> 00:34:23,805
The person she likes vanished into thin air.

442
00:34:23,875 --> 00:34:25,035
How could she possibly be okay?

443
00:34:26,805 --> 00:34:30,045
Man, she's a complete wreck. I was worried she'd collapse.

444
00:34:31,315 --> 00:34:32,315
And you...

445
00:34:32,885 --> 00:34:33,885
Are you okay?

446
00:34:34,415 --> 00:34:35,485
I'm fine.

447
00:34:36,155 --> 00:34:37,615
You're the one going through a hard time because of me.

448
00:34:40,055 --> 00:34:41,055
Sorry.

449
00:34:41,625 --> 00:34:43,225
He always says he's fine.

450
00:34:43,795 --> 00:34:45,765
I must be crazy for even asking.

451
00:34:46,465 --> 00:34:47,465
Hey, you too, man.

452
00:34:48,195 --> 00:34:49,395
Don't suffer for too long before you come back.

453
00:34:50,035 --> 00:34:51,035
I'll make you a meal.

454
00:34:52,135 --> 00:34:53,135
I'm hanging up.

455
00:35:21,265 --> 00:35:24,465
Unable to connect. You will be forwarded to voicemail.

456
00:35:26,665 --> 00:35:28,135
What is the reason for all this?

457
00:35:28,535 --> 00:35:30,605
Shouldn't you at least give me a reason?

458
00:35:31,105 --> 00:35:33,745
Eun Hwan, were you always this selfish and irresponsible?

459
00:35:36,415 --> 00:35:39,315
Forget it. From now on, wherever you are,

460
00:35:40,815 --> 00:35:42,515
I don't care what you do.

461
00:35:43,785 --> 00:35:44,955
So don't ever contact me again.

462
00:35:47,285 --> 00:35:48,285
Your message has been saved.

463
00:35:50,395 --> 00:35:52,025
Did you go on a trip somewhere?

464
00:35:52,865 --> 00:35:54,665
It must be a really great place...

465
00:35:55,265 --> 00:35:56,565
if you left without a word to me.

466
00:35:58,535 --> 00:35:59,535
You should have taken me with you.

467
00:36:00,565 --> 00:36:01,565
That's so cheap.

468
00:36:03,005 --> 00:36:04,675
Can't you at least call me?

469
00:36:05,905 --> 00:36:06,945
I'm so...

470
00:36:10,115 --> 00:36:11,615
I'm so worried.

471
00:36:13,385 --> 00:36:15,885
Cha Eun Hwan, you're...

472
00:36:17,155 --> 00:36:19,585
You're such a jerk. A complete jerk.

473
00:36:25,525 --> 00:36:27,025
Fine, have a great life all by yourself.

474
00:36:27,995 --> 00:36:28,995
Just you wait until you get back.

475
00:36:29,795 --> 00:36:31,565
I won't let you get away with this.

476
00:36:32,635 --> 00:36:33,635
Next message.

477
00:36:35,005 --> 00:36:36,235
When you come back,

478
00:36:37,205 --> 00:36:38,775
I'll forgive you for everything.

479
00:36:39,805 --> 00:36:41,075
So, please just come back.

480
00:36:42,445 --> 00:36:44,015
I miss you so much.

481
00:36:45,345 --> 00:36:48,015
No more messages.

482
00:36:58,625 --> 00:36:59,825
(Dong Gyeong Kitchen)

483
00:36:59,895 --> 00:37:00,895
Welcome.

484
00:37:02,495 --> 00:37:04,735
Have you heard from him?

485
00:37:06,265 --> 00:37:07,265
No.

486
00:37:23,515 --> 00:37:26,125
Here's your order. Enjoy.

487
00:37:30,695 --> 00:37:31,695
Still nothing?

488
00:37:32,665 --> 00:37:33,795
Yes, well...

489
00:37:42,135 --> 00:37:45,035
This is driving me crazy.

490
00:37:48,045 --> 00:37:49,045
Yes, we're closed now.

491
00:37:52,375 --> 00:37:53,385
Still...

492
00:38:15,405 --> 00:38:16,575
You have soju here, right?

493
00:38:16,975 --> 00:38:17,975
Soju?

494
00:38:18,505 --> 00:38:19,575
You mean, not sparkling water?

495
00:39:07,885 --> 00:39:10,225
Hey. Come on out, Cha Eun Hwan.

496
00:39:10,795 --> 00:39:12,765
You jerk. You're in there, aren't you?

497
00:39:13,495 --> 00:39:14,495
You selfish jerk.

498
00:39:15,095 --> 00:39:16,535
You think I can't find you?

499
00:39:17,065 --> 00:39:20,105
You jerk, I said come out. Come out.

500
00:39:31,175 --> 00:39:32,175
You jerk.

501
00:39:33,185 --> 00:39:35,515
Are you having fun toying with my heart?

502
00:39:40,185 --> 00:39:42,355
I passed. I got the part.

503
00:39:44,155 --> 00:39:47,295
One, two, three.

504
00:39:47,365 --> 00:39:49,095
Friends hold hands when they hang out these days.

505
00:39:57,105 --> 00:39:58,705
You shouldn't have been so nice to me.

506
00:40:01,045 --> 00:40:02,305
You shouldn't have made me fall for you.

507
00:40:04,215 --> 00:40:05,575
If you were just going to disappear like this,

508
00:40:07,345 --> 00:40:08,745
what am I supposed to do?

509
00:40:21,965 --> 00:40:23,094
Ladies and gentlemen,

510
00:40:23,095 --> 00:40:24,534
our plane will be arriving...

511
00:40:24,535 --> 00:40:26,835
at Incheon International Airport shortly.

512
00:40:26,905 --> 00:40:28,835
Please be seated and ensure your seatbelts...

513
00:40:28,905 --> 00:40:32,175
are securely fastened. Thank you.

514
00:40:40,645 --> 00:40:41,715
Watch out.

515
00:40:44,385 --> 00:40:45,385
Ji An.

516
00:40:51,895 --> 00:40:53,825
Where are you right now? Ji An got hurt,

517
00:40:53,895 --> 00:40:55,125
and she's asking for you.

518
00:41:01,205 --> 00:41:07,845
(Regional Emergency Medical Center)

519
00:41:11,475 --> 00:41:13,784
I'm here. Where should I go? How is Ji An...

520
00:41:13,785 --> 00:41:17,485
I'm sorry. I had no other choice.

521
00:41:31,665 --> 00:41:32,695
Your injuries...

522
00:41:33,905 --> 00:41:34,905
Are you okay?

523
00:41:38,075 --> 00:41:39,675
You jerk.

524
00:41:54,485 --> 00:41:56,525
Did you have a nice trip?

525
00:41:58,325 --> 00:41:59,325
You're not angry?

526
00:42:00,365 --> 00:42:01,425
I can tell...

527
00:42:02,095 --> 00:42:03,465
how sorry you are.

528
00:42:04,935 --> 00:42:05,935
Then...

529
00:42:06,265 --> 00:42:07,965
why did you do something you'd feel so sorry about?

530
00:42:11,305 --> 00:42:12,405
Are you...

531
00:42:13,305 --> 00:42:14,805
upset with me about something?

532
00:42:19,115 --> 00:42:20,145
Or...

533
00:42:21,185 --> 00:42:22,745
did I do something wrong?

534
00:42:23,785 --> 00:42:24,785
No.

535
00:42:25,485 --> 00:42:26,555
It's not that.

536
00:42:34,065 --> 00:42:35,125
It's just that...

537
00:42:36,435 --> 00:42:37,765
I've been having a hard time.

538
00:42:40,835 --> 00:42:42,235
I mean, from my perspective,

539
00:42:43,205 --> 00:42:44,635
helping you with your comeback,

540
00:42:45,235 --> 00:42:47,875
playing manager, which I'm not cut out for,

541
00:42:48,075 --> 00:42:49,345
and channelling your emotions...

542
00:42:50,575 --> 00:42:51,815
Of course it wasn't going to be easy.

543
00:42:52,645 --> 00:42:54,545
So you were cleared of the bullying accusation.

544
00:42:55,445 --> 00:42:57,215
And since you started acting well without me,

545
00:42:57,855 --> 00:42:59,315
I thought it was the right time to leave.

546
00:43:00,155 --> 00:43:01,385
If that was too sudden,

547
00:43:02,825 --> 00:43:03,855
I'm sorry about that.

548
00:43:05,355 --> 00:43:06,365
All that time...

549
00:43:08,665 --> 00:43:10,935
Was being with me...

550
00:43:13,235 --> 00:43:14,335
that difficult for you?

551
00:43:23,815 --> 00:43:24,845
I see.

552
00:43:27,985 --> 00:43:29,245
But I enjoyed our time together.

553
00:43:34,655 --> 00:43:35,655
So...

554
00:43:36,155 --> 00:43:37,895
Did you enjoy your trip?

555
00:43:38,525 --> 00:43:39,695
Where did you go?

556
00:43:40,325 --> 00:43:42,625
The beach? The mountains?

557
00:43:44,535 --> 00:43:45,565
Just...

558
00:43:47,005 --> 00:43:48,005
a fishing spot.

559
00:43:49,535 --> 00:43:50,575
A fishing spot?

560
00:43:51,535 --> 00:43:52,675
It's a place I often went to with my father...

561
00:43:54,675 --> 00:43:56,415
when I was a kid.

562
00:43:57,575 --> 00:43:59,175
I suddenly felt the urge to go there.

563
00:44:02,415 --> 00:44:03,455
That must have been nice.

564
00:44:06,085 --> 00:44:08,385
So nice that you didn't even think of me.

565
00:44:10,225 --> 00:44:11,955
You could have at least reached out.

566
00:44:12,725 --> 00:44:15,995
- So I wouldn't have to worry. - What exactly are we?

567
00:44:17,565 --> 00:44:19,095
I'm not your manager anymore.

568
00:44:19,865 --> 00:44:21,004
We're not in any kind of relationship.

569
00:44:21,005 --> 00:44:23,635
If a scandal breaks out because we're messaging each other...

570
00:44:24,975 --> 00:44:29,045
You have to be careful after your difficult comeback.

571
00:44:29,345 --> 00:44:30,715
Do you really think that?

572
00:44:32,075 --> 00:44:33,545
That we're nothing to each other?

573
00:44:45,195 --> 00:44:47,295
If we're nothing, then why are you here today?

574
00:44:48,025 --> 00:44:50,365
When you hear that someone who means nothing to you got hurt,

575
00:44:51,135 --> 00:44:53,005
do you always come running like a madman?

576
00:44:58,305 --> 00:45:01,475
Even if it hadn't been you, Yu Ji An, I would've done the same.

577
00:45:01,945 --> 00:45:02,945
So,

578
00:45:03,445 --> 00:45:06,845
- don't read too much into it. - Then what was that kiss about?

579
00:45:10,085 --> 00:45:13,155
Does a kiss really mean that much between us?

580
00:45:16,255 --> 00:45:17,425
That kiss was...

581
00:45:17,725 --> 00:45:19,455
just my way of saying goodbye.

582
00:45:20,765 --> 00:45:21,765
Are we clear?

583
00:45:23,635 --> 00:45:25,195
Then why can't you look me in the eye?

584
00:45:26,505 --> 00:45:28,865
It's because you don't want me to see how you feel, isn't it?

585
00:45:32,005 --> 00:45:33,144
- That's... - Do you know what the...

586
00:45:33,145 --> 00:45:34,375
hardest part for me right now is?

587
00:45:36,005 --> 00:45:37,715
The fact I know that every word you're saying...

588
00:45:39,375 --> 00:45:40,915
is a lie.

589
00:45:42,645 --> 00:45:43,855
I know it all.

590
00:45:44,485 --> 00:45:45,755
And I can feel it all.

591
00:45:47,355 --> 00:45:49,385
So why are you so desperate to push me away?

592
00:45:49,795 --> 00:45:50,795
Why?

593
00:45:57,895 --> 00:45:59,565
You really don't know why?

594
00:46:02,105 --> 00:46:04,305
Someone who knows my every feeling.

595
00:46:06,645 --> 00:46:08,475
Don't you think that would be terrifying for me?

596
00:46:21,925 --> 00:46:23,525
I know you're lying.

597
00:46:49,285 --> 00:46:52,285
(JJ Actors Entertainment)

598
00:46:54,355 --> 00:46:55,555
(Cha Eun Hwan, Therapist, Tok Tok Mental Care)

599
00:46:55,625 --> 00:46:57,925
(Observation: Ji An is exhibiting considerably open emotions.)

600
00:46:58,725 --> 00:47:00,865
(CEO Kim)

601
00:47:07,705 --> 00:47:10,075
(Controversial Therapy Method: "Imaginary Revenge" Psychotherapy)

602
00:47:15,145 --> 00:47:17,245
(CEO Kim Jun Sik)

603
00:47:22,315 --> 00:47:23,354
The party you are trying to reach is unavailable.

604
00:47:23,355 --> 00:47:25,055
You will be connected to their voicemail...

605
00:47:27,425 --> 00:47:28,685
She's ignoring my calls?

606
00:47:29,755 --> 00:47:30,755
Darn it.

607
00:47:31,725 --> 00:47:33,595
What, does she expect me to take the fall for this alone?

608
00:47:37,835 --> 00:47:38,835
CEO Kim.

609
00:47:39,135 --> 00:47:41,465
What? What is it?

610
00:47:42,335 --> 00:47:44,605
Two of the rookie actors we signed last month...

611
00:47:45,375 --> 00:47:46,845
have filed a lawsuit to terminate their contracts.

612
00:47:53,415 --> 00:47:55,085
Those pathetic little punks.

613
00:47:55,485 --> 00:47:56,485
And...

614
00:47:56,615 --> 00:47:57,615
(District Court)

615
00:47:57,815 --> 00:47:58,815
Han Yi Jin, too.

616
00:48:01,325 --> 00:48:02,325
What?

617
00:48:03,795 --> 00:48:04,795
Han Yi Jin?

618
00:48:09,495 --> 00:48:10,635
(Complaint)

619
00:48:10,695 --> 00:48:12,465
(Plaintiff: Han Yi Jin, Defendant: CEO Kim Jun Sik)

620
00:48:16,135 --> 00:48:17,435
(Suit to Confirm Exclusive Contract Termination)

621
00:48:18,635 --> 00:48:20,075
(CEO Kim Jun Sik)

622
00:48:20,375 --> 00:48:21,375
Darn it.

623
00:48:24,345 --> 00:48:25,715
(For Sale)

624
00:48:26,375 --> 00:48:27,715
All right, great. Let's do it.

625
00:48:28,185 --> 00:48:29,855
Wait, you're really going to sign right now?

626
00:48:29,915 --> 00:48:31,315
You should look at a few more places.

627
00:48:31,385 --> 00:48:34,725
- The location isn't great. - But I have the skills.

628
00:48:35,355 --> 00:48:36,455
So what's the worry?

629
00:48:37,325 --> 00:48:39,054
Now that I hear you talk, I'm reminded...

630
00:48:39,055 --> 00:48:40,495
of what a jerk you've always been.

631
00:48:40,565 --> 00:48:42,695
(For Rent or Sale)

632
00:48:42,765 --> 00:48:44,565
I want to start working as soon as possible.

633
00:48:45,135 --> 00:48:47,305
It'll keep my mind off things.

634
00:48:52,075 --> 00:48:53,075
What?

635
00:48:53,375 --> 00:48:55,905
The forecast didn't say anything about rain today.

636
00:48:59,745 --> 00:49:02,285
I can't breathe.

637
00:49:03,815 --> 00:49:05,655
Just do exactly as I do, okay?

638
00:49:06,755 --> 00:49:08,625
Breathe in. One, two.

639
00:49:09,785 --> 00:49:11,395
Breathe out. Three, four.

640
00:49:21,765 --> 00:49:23,275
I'm not your manager anymore.

641
00:49:24,235 --> 00:49:25,504
We're not in any kind of relationship.

642
00:49:25,505 --> 00:49:27,975
If a scandal breaks out because we're messaging each other...

643
00:49:31,445 --> 00:49:33,315
(Mom)

644
00:49:41,685 --> 00:49:44,995
(Mom)

645
00:49:45,055 --> 00:49:46,565
(Tuesday, March 24)

646
00:50:04,775 --> 00:50:07,715
Hello? Could you please open the door?

647
00:50:07,785 --> 00:50:09,315
Hello? Is anybody there?

648
00:50:10,685 --> 00:50:12,155
Please, open the door.

649
00:50:24,965 --> 00:50:25,965
Ji An.

650
00:50:26,335 --> 00:50:28,205
The shoot's cancelled because of the rain.

651
00:50:28,305 --> 00:50:30,635
(Actress Yu Ji An's Dressing Room)

652
00:50:31,035 --> 00:50:32,035
What the...

653
00:50:33,205 --> 00:50:34,245
Is it broken?

654
00:50:38,015 --> 00:50:39,015
Oh, man.

655
00:50:39,875 --> 00:50:42,215
It's raining out. This is so annoying.

656
00:50:43,285 --> 00:50:44,855
Ji An, are you in there?

657
00:50:46,055 --> 00:50:47,125
Ji An, are you okay?

658
00:50:49,185 --> 00:50:50,195
Ji An.

659
00:50:57,495 --> 00:50:58,495
Pick up.

660
00:50:59,765 --> 00:51:01,635
Yes, is this maintenance? The door here is broken.

661
00:51:01,705 --> 00:51:02,735
Please send someone quickly.

662
00:51:03,375 --> 00:51:04,705
Right now.

663
00:51:05,475 --> 00:51:06,905
Ji An is in there, and she is claustrophobic.

664
00:51:07,975 --> 00:51:09,275
Help me.

665
00:51:11,115 --> 00:51:12,375
Help me.

666
00:51:14,015 --> 00:51:15,315
Help me.

667
00:51:16,385 --> 00:51:17,555
Help me.

668
00:51:18,715 --> 00:51:22,485
Kiddo, if you don't want to do this, you can just say so.

669
00:51:22,825 --> 00:51:24,225
No one will be mad at you.

670
00:51:25,955 --> 00:51:28,395
You'll be all by yourself in this warehouse set.

671
00:51:28,895 --> 00:51:29,925
Aren't you scared?

672
00:51:32,365 --> 00:51:34,635
No. I'm not scared.

673
00:51:34,765 --> 00:51:37,575
If at any point you get scared or feel like you're in danger,

674
00:51:37,835 --> 00:51:39,135
just scream for help.

675
00:51:39,575 --> 00:51:43,305
And I'll come running like Superman to save you.

676
00:51:43,645 --> 00:51:45,775
- Got it? - Okay.

677
00:51:47,285 --> 00:51:48,285
Okay.

678
00:51:52,285 --> 00:51:54,155
Kiddo, stay with me.

679
00:51:54,685 --> 00:51:55,685
Kiddo.

680
00:51:58,155 --> 00:51:59,355
Are you okay?

681
00:51:59,755 --> 00:52:00,925
Help me.

682
00:52:02,295 --> 00:52:03,465
Help me.

683
00:52:03,865 --> 00:52:07,105
Okay. I'll definitely save you.

684
00:52:09,505 --> 00:52:11,175
Don't lose consciousness, okay?

